TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the transposed (CaddG) and add the 5th note as necessary.

TIP:  In the intro, (CaddG) is just (C) with pinky added to bottom string/3rd fret.  (C7) is just (C) with pinky added to 3rd string/3rd fret.  For (C7/F), which follows (C7), just roll your index finger over to cover the bottom string/1st fret <f> like you do when playing a normal (F).  So when you're playing (C)(CaddG)(C)(C7)(C7/F) you start with (C), add pinky to bottom string, lift, then to the 3rd string, and then roll over to mini-barred the <f>, then to the (Am).
 
          
